cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VanToVault Open Housing Data: Foothold Index, Down Payment Assistance Survey, and Pittsburgh Short-Term Rental Census"
message: "If you use these datasets, please cite them using the metadata below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "VanToVault"
    alias: "Stephan D."
    email: vantovault@gmail.com
    website: "https://vantovault.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vantovault-stack/open-housing-data"
url: "https://vantovault.com/open-data/"
abstract: >-
  Open datasets on buying a two-to-four unit home as an owner-occupant across 83 US metro areas.
  The Foothold Index screens 23,424 two-to-four unit listings against seven absolute tests to find
  where a first-time buyer with limited savings can own for no more than the cost of renting. The
  Down Payment Assistance Survey answers, metro by metro, whether an owner-occupant can use down
  payment assistance on a two-to-four unit home, distinguishing programs that were found, programs
  confirmed absent, and cases where eligibility could not be confirmed. The Pittsburgh Short-Term
  Rental Census is a hand-checked, listing-level count of short-term and mid-term rentals in
  Lawrenceville and Bloomfield as of August 2026, with boundary-uncertainty flags and three rate windows.
keywords:
  - housing affordability
  - house hacking
  - owner-occupant
  - down payment assistance
  - first-time homebuyer
  - multifamily
  - short-term rentals
  - Pittsburgh
  - open data
